  "effort_guide_note": "api_default is what the API runs when effort is omitted. routine is for chat and short, well-specified tasks; agentic is the starting level for multistep coding and tool use; hardest is worth its cost only where a gain was measured on your own tasks. stops_early_at lists the levels at which the model is documented to end a long task early, so a long-horizon prompt needs explicit completion instructions there.",
  "prompting_rules": {
    "effort-not-budget": "Use adaptive thinking and set depth with `output_config.effort`. `thinking: {type: \"enabled\", budget_tokens: N}` is rejected.",
    "thinking-always-on": "`thinking: {type: \"disabled\"}` is rejected. Lower `effort` instead; Sonnet 5.5 accepts `{type: \"between_tools\"}` at `high` or below.",
    "no-sampling-params": "Omit temperature, top_p and top_k. Fable, Mythos and Opus reject any value; Sonnet 5.5 and Haiku 5.5 reject every non-default value.",
    "no-reasoning-in-reply": "Do not ask for raw reasoning or chain of thought in the reply text: the request can be declined with the `reasoning_extraction` refusal category. Read `display: \"summarized\"` thinking blocks instead.",
    "finish-the-task": "The model can end a long task early at the effort levels in `stops_early_at`. Give a long-horizon agent explicit completion instructions (a `# Finishing work` block).",
    "append-only-history": "Keep the conversation append-only and pass thinking blocks back unchanged. Editing or dropping earlier turns invalidates preserved thinking.",
    "no-forced-tool-choice": "tool_choice `any` and `tool` are rejected. Use `auto` and name the tool in the prompt.",
    "no-prefill": "Assistant-turn prefill is rejected. Describe the format or use structured outputs."
  },
